    "summary": "The real action arrives this weekend. Saturday brings a brief lull before an icy southerly blasts up the South Island early Sunday, potentially dumping 5-15+cm across the Southern Lakes and 10-30cm in Canterbury. Mt Ruapehu gets its share later Sunday, although severe gales and heavy rain beforehand will make for a pretty atrocious day.",
