      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with an overcast day expected, a few patches of sunshine breaking through, and increasing wind that may affect lift operations at times. There's been 6 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently 3°C with winds around 23 km/h gusting to 35 km/h. Classic spring conditions are on offer, firm underfoot to start before softening as temperatures warm up. All 10 of 10 lifts are open, with all 9 of 9 park features and all 10 of 10 terrain zones open. Main Basin and Valley View open from 8:30am, with Captains, Willows, Soho and the T-Bar following from 9am. The Uninvited Park Jam, a female-only snowboard event, is on today in McPark, with National Points Racing also running on Tail Race, closed to the public while racing is underway. Olympic Pipe closes at 12:45pm today. The access road is chain-free but chains must be carried, with an active road hazard advisory in place. The spring Pines Shuttle and bus schedule begins 1 October. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
