      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, kicking off the final Saturday of the season with a mild spring morning and fun snow conditions. There's been no new snowfall in the past 24 hours, with the natural base holding at 150 cm at the top of Home Basin; it's currently 3°C with winds around 21 km/h gusting to 35 km/h, sunny with plenty of high fives on the mountain. Saddle Track access may close within the hour due to warming temperatures, though the Saddle Chair will keep running regardless. All 3 of 3 lifts and all 11 of 11 groomed trails are open, with 8 of 9 terrain zones open; only Motatapu Chutes is on hold. Home Basin runs 8:30am–4pm and Saddle Basin 9am–3:30pm today. Kiri the Kea's birthday party is on the mountain today, with a scavenger hunt, face painting, dress-ups and cake at noon, plus a BBQ on the Sundeck; fancy dress is encouraged for the final weekend of the season. The access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle running from the bottom of the access road. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
